WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
It's Friday, welcome to Tesla Short's time,

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.080
daily episode 492 from May 29th, 2026.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.980
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.860
Let's close out the week with today's Tesla news.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.000
Texas granting Tesla commercial driverless rights,

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.040
shifts its robot taxi plans

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.800
from supervised testing into paid operation.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.200
Tesla self-certified its software at SAE level four,

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.300
securing commercial driverless rights in the state.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.040
The filing covers operation without a safety driver

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.240
in permitted zones.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.160
This step allows paid robot taxi service

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.060
to begin once vehicles are deployed.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.340
The authorization followed separate state-level

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.080
framework updates on autonomy.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.080
This moves the program past pure testing

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.360
into a regulated commercial environment.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.460
The next milestones are initial fleet size

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.660
and first revenue generating trips.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.060
While Texas opens the door to commercial use,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.020
real world supervised performance on long routes

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.960
is already being tested elsewhere.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.680
A Tesla completed a coast to coast run

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.280
from Vancouver to Halifax,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.840
covering 3,760 miles with zero human input

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.660
under FSD supervised.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.760
The trip demonstrates the system's ability

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.680
to manage long distance highway

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.820
and urban segments without intervention.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.760
This milestone adds real world unsupervised

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.640
capable data to the training set

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.700
ahead of broader regulatory reviews.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.880
The route covered highways, rural roads, and urban streets.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.540
Next data point to watch is whether similar cross-border runs

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.780
appear in Europe following recent approvals.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.640
The same supervised software is also showing incremental

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.880
improvements on shorter mixed roads in the latest release.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.300
Version 14.3.3 completed a mixed route

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.060
that included turnpikes, winding back roads,

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.900
and small town streets without driver takeover.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.140
The drive covered varied speed limits

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.480
and road surfaces in a single session.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.440
This performance shows incremental gains in handling edge cases

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.980
that earlier versions flagged for intervention.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:11.220
A 130 mile trip was completed without driver takeover

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.200
across varied speeds and surfaces.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:18.040
Watch for wider V14.3.3 distribution numbers

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.040
in the coming weeks.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.660
The same supervised software is also showing

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.400
incremental improvements on shorter mixed routes

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.520
in the latest release.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.840
Estonia became the third EU country

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.520
to clear FSD supervised after the Netherlands and Lithuania.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.680
The transport authority accepted the Dutch type

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.700
approval documentation for the system.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.420
This expands the supervised feature to another market

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.640
without requiring separate local testing.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.980
The move continues the pattern of rapid European

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.760
regulatory acceptance seen in recent months.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.820
European regulators are also moving forward

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.440
with the supervised system.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.280
Not everyone close to the training data

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.740
shares the same confidence in the system's readiness.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.500
Trainers who label FSD data reportedly told interviewers

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.400
they would not ride in an unsupervised robot taxi

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.460
even for payment.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.620
Their stance highlights a gap between claimed safety statistics

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.580
and the confidence of those closest to the training process.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.900
Tesla will need to close that perception gap

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:23.220
before regulators and riders accept driverless service

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:23.840
at scale.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.400
Data labelers told interviewers they would not ride

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.260
in a driverless robot taxi even if paid.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.560
This highlights a gap between Tesla's safety claims

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.300
and internal confidence levels.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.820
Stepping back from daily headlines,

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.140
the Canada Drive raises a deeper question

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:44.440
about what actually remains before unsupervised operation.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:49.360
The 3,700 mega mile trip occurred on public roads

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.480
that include highways, rural routes, and urban streets

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.500
without a single driver takeover.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.860
That distance exceeds most documented supervised demonstrations

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.780
and supplies a new volume of edge case data

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.300
that earlier short tests could not capture.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.580
The result suggests the software's prediction models

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.340
have reached a level where long duration reliability

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.480
rather than isolated maneuvers is becoming

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.820
the measurable constraint.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.320
Tesla's approach of collecting fleet scale miles

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.160
before seeking broader approval

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.860
therefore gains practical weight.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.600
If the same data pipeline that produced the Canada run

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.120
